      "text": "The Vegas Golden Knights, constructors of a decisive playoff run, overcame the Colorado Avalanche's crafted structure being stripped of its key components through injury. After a mid-project creative overhaul saw John Tortorella, architect of a 7-0-1 closing surge, installed as coach, he engineered sequential playoff victories. In the Western Conference Final, the Knights executed a flawless defensive composition, scoring twice and limiting the opponent's scoring in the final game to one goal. This finished a perfectly orchestrated series sweep, validating their build and securing championship series qualification.",
